<!-- "ESRB Everyone" edition (2026-06-26): a standalone drug- and alcohol-free
     version of VSG. No mention of drugs/alcohol by peers, bosses, or the player,
     and none of the substance mechanics. The job DRUG TEST is kept (a real
     workplace lesson) but the player always passes it, because nothing in this
     pack can ever raise the player's Cannabinoids (DrugTestLogic passes when < 30).

     Substance handling uses the SINGLE FPC `substance` content flag, enforced here
     for the first time: substances appear only when an active pack DECLARES
     content_flags="substance" (or no pack is active = base game). This pack simply
     OMITS the flag, so ContentPack.SuppressSubstances is true and the game hides
     all substance content. That is the whole switch; there is no separate
     "no_substance" flag.

     From data alone (no recompile): characters.xml forces every NPC
     alcoholic="false" stoner="false" (absent = 50% random in CharacterManager, so
     it MUST be explicit); jobs.xml zeroes every boss chance_drunk/chance_high (incl.
     replacements) and keeps drug_test="true". With traits + boss-states neutralized
     and the substance flag off, every substance EVENT (drinking/smoking convergences,
     hidden-substance, party beer/weed) goes dormant. Three code gates on
     ContentPack.SuppressSubstances remove the only non-data-driven bits (the player's
     Suggest-Weed/Alcohol menu, the apartment No-Drugs/No-Smoking policy text, and the
     "came in drunk/high" memory lines).

     NOTE: this removes the SUBSTANCE axis of an ESRB Everyone rating; the VIOLENCE
     axis (fights / goons / bikers) is separate and unaddressed here. -->
<manifest name="ESRB Everyone">
	<description>A drug- and alcohol-free version. No substance use or talk by anyone; the job still drug-tests you, and you always pass.</description>
	<!-- Standalone product: keep a SEPARATE save/replay database from the base /play
	     game (per-user save lives under everyone/users/<id>/), matching the separate
	     /everyone account namespace. See ContentPack.saveScope + AccountManager. -->
	<tuning save_scope="everyone"/>
</manifest>
